    <string name="privacy_button">Privacy and permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_message">DroidClean sends no personal data anywhere. Its only outgoing connection queries GitHub\'s public API to check for a newer version.\n\nWhy each permission:\n\n• All files access — read and delete the files you select. Scoped storage makes this impossible otherwise.\n• Usage access — compute real app sizes and last-used dates.\n• App list — count installed apps and spot leftovers from uninstalled ones.\n• Install apps — install the downloaded update.\n• Notifications — tell you an update is ready.\n• Internet — query GitHub Releases.\n\nCrash reports stay on the device until you choose to share them.</string>

    <string name="onboarding_title">Welcome to DroidClean</string>
    <string name="onboarding_message">DroidClean never deletes anything without showing it to you first.\n\nThe scan lists what can go; you tick, you confirm. Your documents go through the system bin, where they stay recoverable.\n\nTo go beyond its own caches, the app needs shared storage access.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_ok">Got it</string>

